{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Problems and Solutions"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Misadventures at the Conference"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le12ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Future Perfect Tense and the Present Perfect Tense: Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future Perfect tense to say that something will be ended, completed or achieved by a particular point in the future. <br/>You use the Present Perfect tense to show a connection between a past event and a present situation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The form of the Future Perfect tense is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "subject + will + have + past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Let's hope the rain <span class=\"strong\">will have stopped</span> by the time we land.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In this example, you hope that when you land, the rain will be finished. Using the Future Perfect tense is like you are looking back in the past from a future point."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use other modal verbs to talk about the future in a less certain way. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">By the time you get home, I may have already cleaned the house.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The form of the Present Perfect is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "subject + have + past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The reservations have been made. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Refer to the chart for a summary of some other commonly used tenses:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Use/Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to tell a story - it makes the action seem more direct (as if it is happening right now)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m standing </span>in line at the grocery store and I realize that I forgot my wallet!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to talk about what people have arranged to do\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Tom <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is going to the airport this afternoon</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to talk about what is happening at the time of speaking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I<span class=\\\"strong\\\">'m just calling </span>him now to see if he is free.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "By the time I get back, I hope this bickering will have stopped."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will have gone to the boardroom several times by the time that happens."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Perfect Modals"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use Perfect modals to refer to different possibilities in the past, present and future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use a Perfect modal:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "1.  from a point of time in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We were worried.  <span class=\"italic\">Someone <span class=\"strong\">might have taken</span> the car</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "2.  to refer back from the present"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">It is nearly eight o'clock</span>. They will have arrived by now."}, {"type": "text", "content": "3. to refer back from the future"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We won't eat until they arrive. They <span class=\"strong\">might not have had</span> lunch.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "4. to refer to past time"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">could have helped</span> her when she asked.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It might have been more enjoyable, if you weren't pretending to be me."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You could have told me about the reservation. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "How could you have forgotten to do that, Boris?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Note: You can use could have (been) to say that it was possible that something happened in the past (but you are not 100% sure)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> It <span class=\"strong\">could have been avoided had</span> Boris been more organized</span>. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "amusing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "entertaining"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It was amusing to say the least and rather eventful."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to recap a business trip."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"content